01. Pick up the patient file from the reception desk.
02. Open the pharmacy storage cabinet.
03. Close the patient room door.
04. Place the wheelchair beside the patient's bed.
05. Pick up the blood pressure monitor from the examination table.
06. Turn off the examination room light.
07. Move the IV stand beside the patient's bed.
08. Place the sanitizer bottle on the reception counter.
09. Pick up the patient file and place it on the nurse station desk.
10. Open the medicine cabinet and retrieve the first aid kit.
11. Pick up the wheelchair and park it near the waiting area.
12. Close the medicine cabinet after placing the thermometer inside.
13. Pick up the medical tray and place it on the examination table.
14. Retrieve the blanket and place it on the patient's bed.
15. Open the supply room door and collect the bandage box.
16. Pick up the clipboard and place it on the doctor's desk.
17. Go to the pharmacy, collect the medicine box, and deliver it to the nurse station.
18. Navigate to the patient room, retrieve the patient file, and return it to the reception desk.
19. Go to the storage room, collect a wheelchair, and place it outside Room 101.
20. Navigate to the examination room, retrieve the stethoscope, and place it on the doctor's desk.
21. Go to the waiting area, collect the abandoned walking stick, and return it to reception.
22. Navigate to the laboratory, collect the sample container, and deliver it to the examination room.
23. Go to the supply room, retrieve a box of gloves, and place it in the nurse station.
24. Navigate to the patient room, collect the used food tray, and place it in the designated collection area.
25. If the wheelchair is available near reception, move it to Room 102; otherwise bring the walking aid.
26. If the medicine cabinet is open, close it before leaving the pharmacy.
27. If the patient's room door is closed, open it before delivering the medical tray.
28. If gloves are unavailable at the nurse station, retrieve a new box from the supply room.
29. If the waiting area contains unattended equipment, return it to the storage room; otherwise inspect the reception desk.
30. If the examination table is occupied, place the medical tray on the side table; otherwise place it on the examination table.
31. If a sanitizer bottle is missing from the reception counter, bring one from the supply room.
32. Transport the medicine box while keeping it upright.
33. Deliver the blood sample container without tilting or dropping it.
34. Move the wheelchair through the corridor without colliding with patients or furniture.
35. Carry the medical tray carefully without disturbing the instruments.
36. Place the oxygen cylinder in the designated area without blocking the emergency exit.
37. Deliver the IV stand while keeping the attached tubing untangled.
38. Move the portable monitor to the examination room without disconnecting its power cable.
39. Collect all patient files from the reception desk, distribute them to the respective examination rooms, and return to the nurse station.
40. Restock the nurse station by collecting gloves, masks, sanitizer, and bandages from the supply room, placing each item in its designated location, and returning to reception.
41. Inspect all patient rooms for misplaced wheelchairs, IV stands, and medical trays, return each item to its designated location, and report completion.
42. Prepare an examination room by bringing a medical tray, placing a blood pressure monitor on the examination table, positioning a chair for the patient, and ensuring the room door is closed.
43. Collect used meal trays from all occupied patient rooms, deliver them to the collection area, sanitize the collection cart, and return it to storage.
44. Inspect the pharmacy, nurse station, waiting area, and examination rooms for open cabinets, misplaced equipment, and missing sanitizer bottles, correct each issue, and return to reception.
45. Prepare the hospital for the next shift by organizing the reception desk, restocking essential supplies, parking all wheelchairs in the designated area, ensuring patient room doors are properly closed, and returning to the nurse station.
